BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN HARRIET ALIDA LYE IN CONVERSATION WITH ASHLEY AUDRAIN
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260610T200000
UID:bm-5435020260610@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/Harriet_A
 lida_Lye_Author_Photo.jpg?cb=1778727080
DESCRIPTION:Join Flying Books and McClelland and Stewart for an evening 
 of conversation with Harriet Alida Lye as she discusses her new book\nMoth
 erclown\nwith Ashley Audrain (bestselling author of\nThe Push\n).\nMotherc
 lown\nexplores the most fundamental and potentially explosive of human rel
 ationships: that of a mother and her daughter.\n\nIn the wake of her fathe
 r’s death\, twenty-one-year-old Elise leaves her hometown of Niagara Fal
 ls to move to Paris\, where she begins training at Chevalier\, an elite ph
 ysical theatre school focused on clown.\n\nLeft behind\, Elise’s mother 
 Catherine is unravelling—grieving\, restless\, and haunted by regret. Wh
 en Elise disappears into Paris\, Catherine follows.\n\nAs Paris works its 
 spell on them both\, old wounds surface and resentments ignite. Can Elise 
 hear her mother without losing herself? Can Catherine face what she has do
 ne—or is she there to swallow her daughter whole?\n\nMotherclown is an e
 lectric novel about art and inheritance\, desire and devotion\, and the fe
 rocious\, vulnerable love between mothers and daughters.\nHARRIET ALIDA LY
 E is the award-winning author of the novels\nLet It Destroy You\nand\nThe 
 Honey Farm\,\nthe memoir\nNatural Killer\n\, and co-author of the picture 
 book S\nerge the Snail Without a Shell.\nHer work has been published in\nT
 he New York Times\, The Globe and Mail\, National Post\, The Happy Reader\
 , Hazlitt\, Vice\, Catapult\n\, and more. She lives in Toronto.
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College Street
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Celebrate the launch of Nowhere with Jon Claytor and special guest
 s\, Ian Roy and José Contreras!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260611T200000
UID:bm-5151120260611@flyingbooks.ca
DESCRIPTION:[Book Launch]\nCome and celebrate the launch of\nNowhere\nwith
  Jon Claytor and special guests\, Ian Roy and José Contreras! This event 
 is free and open to the public.\nA hilarious and sinister reflection on gr
 owing up in a world where monsters are real\, Nowhere is a dreamlike medit
 ation on adolescence and the absurdity of small-town life.\n \nJon will be
  reading from this unforgettable graphic novel\, Ian will be reading from 
 his brand new short story collection\,\nAstrid\, Aghast\n\, and singer-son
 gwriter José will play a short set and musical accompaniment to the eveni
 ng’s readings.\nAbout the Authors:\nJON CLAYTOR is a graphic novelist\, 
 painter\, and writer. Born in San Francisco\, he lived and worked in sever
 al Canadian cities\, including Halifax\, Vancouver\, Montreal\, and Toront
 o\, before settling in Sackville\, New Brunswick.\nClaytor’s work ranges
  from oil painting and watercolour to comics. He has had solo exhibitions 
 at galleries in Montreal\, Toronto\, Los Angeles\, and throughout the Mari
 times. He has also written and illustrated stories for CBC Radio\, the Fry
 e Festival\, and the website ruralharmreduction.com.\nIAN ROY is a writer\
 , screen printer\, and educator. His work has appeared in numerous magazin
 es and journals\, including\nThe Antigonish Review\, Arc\, Geist\, Long Co
 n Magazine\, Maisonneuve\,\nand\nThe New Quarterly.\nIan is the author of 
 six books\, including the short story collection\,\nPeople Leaving\,\nwhic
 h was short-listed for both the City of Ottawa Book Award and the Upper Ca
 nada Writers’ Craft Award.
LOCATION:Flying Books\, 784 College St.
URL:https://flyingbooks.ca/events
X-SOURCE:Flying Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JOIN US FOR OUR JUNE FICTION BOOK CLUB:
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260622T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260623T203000
UID:bm-5435920260622@flyingbooks.ca
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/8102716/June_Book
 club_.png?cb=1779283324
DESCRIPTION:[Book Club]\nJoin us for a discussion of the novel\,\nSisters 
 in Yellow\nby one of the great writers of her generation\, Mieko Kawakami\
 nFrom the award-winning author of\nBreasts and Eggs\,\ncomes a bold novel 
 of sacrifice and the tumultuous bonds of sisterhood\, set in the gritty To
 kyo of the 1990s.\n\nHana is fifteen years old\, lives with her mother\, h
 as no money\, and no security. Kimiko is older\, a bright light in Hana’
 s dark world. Together they set up a bar. Suddenly Hana has a job she love
 s\, friends to share her days with\, and the glittering promise of money. 
 She feels like a normal girl.\nBut in the narrow alleys of Sangenjaya\, no
 thing is as it seems. Soon all of Hana’s hope\, her optimism\, and her d
 rive will be pushed to the limit . . .\nSisters in Yellow\nis a story of e
 nduring friendship\, deep betrayal\, and a masterpiece of teenage dreams a
 nd adult cruelties.\nJoin us on Monday\, June 22 or Tuesday\, June 23 for 
 some thrilling conversation. We hope to see you there.\nYour book club tic
 ket includes:\nA glass of wine (or another beverage of your choice).\nA th
 oughtful conversation with our brilliant moderator\, Lee Suksi.\nA $20 cre
 dit toward any book in the shop.\nGET YOUR TICKETS HERE!\nA few details:\n
 Ticket price includes HST and fees.\n$20 book credit is valid on the night
  of attendance only (non-refundable and non-transferable).\nWine is served
  on the night of the event (ID required).\nTickets are non-refundable with
 in 7 days of the event\; due to limited capacity and planning\, we’re no
 t able to transfer tickets to future book club sessions.
